       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 600 mg daily is three times the FDA maximum of 200 mg/day. Doses that high raise the risk of serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, and seizures. Your patient has normal kidney and liver function, so nothing about them would justify a dose that high.\n\nDid you mean a different dose? Typical adult dosing is:\n- **Depression, OCD, or anxiety disorders:** start at 25\u201350 mg once daily, then titrate by 25\u201350 mg at intervals of at least a week. The usual range is 50\u2013200 mg/day.\n- **PTSD or panic disorder:** start at 25 mg once daily, then increase to 50 mg after a week. The maximum is 200 mg/day.\n\nTell me the dose you want, such as 50 mg or 100 mg PO once daily, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 600 mg for a specific reason, tell me the clinical rationale. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy or psychiatry first, and I can add a note to the order."
